{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466293-goddess-influences","id":1466293,"title":"Goddess' Influences","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-02T09:52:04-07:00","id":1466293,"title":"Goddess' Influences","content":"In the rocky highland of an island dwelt a tribe predating the Celts. They followed their own pastoral pursuits, raided sparingly, and fiercely defended their patch of stony earth. They worshipped their goddess, who dwelt in the mountain at the center of their land. This spirit fed off their worship and blessed them with fertility and protection. <br /> <br /> Centuries passed, and waves of Romans, Normans, Frenchmen, and Englishman lapped against their hills. The tribe remained, resistant to change but not impervious to it. Their prayers to deity became charms for luck or to ward off evil. The stone circles weathered, overgrown. But the goddess remained, and a small remnant of her priesthood still supplicates on behalf of the forgetful villagers.<br /> <br /> The locals are still agrarian, bound by identity, wary of outsiders, and highly superstitious. The goddess spirit, though weaker than she once was, is still a major force in the local spirit court. My question is this: what would be some appropriate Influences for the spirit? The Ephemeral Influences book gave me some ideas, but I'm not satisfied that I've captured the powers of a localized goddess. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T10:33:21-07:00","id":1466299,"title":"","content":"Life and earth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T10:54:42-07:00","id":1466300,"title":"","content":"Mountain, Agriculture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T14:49:59-07:00","id":1466337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466293-goddess-influences?p=1466300#post1466300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mountain, Agriculture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the right idea. Bearing in mind that it's a highland, it could be cattle more specifically than agriculture... Though actually I don't know how common that was before the modern-era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T14:51:04-07:00","id":1466338,"title":"","content":"Fertility, to begin with, for animals and plants. But you need to define her better to come up with Influences. How's the cult? How's her myth? How's their rituals?<br /> <br /> If this is a Shadow Spirit, then this Goddes was largely defined by her followers and their beliefs, and that can be a bunch of different things. Sex? House? War? Love? Secrets? Magic? Death? Light? Night? We have everything and then some the world around when it comes to fertility goddesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T18:03:32-07:00","id":1466360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466293-goddess-influences?p=1466338#post1466338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If this is a Shadow Spirit, then this Goddes was largely defined by her followers and their beliefs, and that can be a bunch of different things. Sex? House? War? Love? Secrets? Magic? Death? Light? Night? We have everything and then some the world around when it comes to fertility goddesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Her followers are a step beyond the usual cunning-folk/witches; they're more of a secretive druid sect. They keep secrets but also try to protect the local folk and maintain harmony between them and the land (and supernatural critters). Their rites of worship at stone circles serve to acknowledge the spirits of earth and sky, and thank the powerful but ambivalent goddess. An earlier version of the cult can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/799082-cofd-diy-mystery-cults?p=1334563#post1334563\">here</a>.<br /> Fertility might be one. She's also associated with ravens and owls (not what one would expect of an earth goddess, perhaps, but really, what deity can really be ground down to one or two narrow spheres?)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T18:20:37-07:00","id":1466364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466293-goddess-influences?p=1466360#post1466360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Her followers are a step beyond the usual cunning-folk/witches; they're more of a secretive druid sect. They keep secrets but also try to protect the local folk and maintain harmony between them and the land (and supernatural critters). Their rites of worship at stone circles serve to acknowledge the spirits of earth and sky, and thank the powerful but ambivalent goddess. An earlier version of the cult can be found <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/799082-cofd-diy-mystery-cults?p=1334563#post1334563&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> Fertility might be one. She's also associated with ravens and owls (not what one would expect of an earth goddess, perhaps, but really, what deity can really be ground down to one or two narrow spheres?)</div> </div> </div> </div>You might as well base the spirit on The Morr\u00edgan and have both Crows and Land/Fertility as its Influences. Whether this tutelary spirit is the \u2018real\u2019 Irish goddess herself could be, as many things in the CofD are, left as a mystery. The spirit herself likely cares not much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T18:23:43-07:00","id":1466366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466293-goddess-influences?p=1466360#post1466360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fertility might be one. She's also associated with ravens and owls (not what one would expect of an earth goddess, perhaps, but really, what deity can really be ground down to one or two narrow spheres?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite the opposite, gods are frequently associated with animals common on their sacred sites, and at an island highland there are bound to be birds. So you have one option right there, birds. Luck seems also like an interesting option.<br /> <br /> For the linked text, the only thing I found odd was the idea of <i>embalming</i>the corpse, then let it to <i>putrefy</i>. That's exactly what doesn't happen to an embalmed corpse. It seems their point is more precisely to not embalm, but let the corpse be taken by the earth and the animals.<br /> <br /> You may consider instead a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky_burial\" target=\"_blank\">Sky Burial</a> practice for them. It seems far more in tune with your intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T19:05:11-07:00","id":1466367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1466293-goddess-influences?p=1466366#post1466366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the linked text, the only thing I found odd was the idea of <i>embalming</i>the corpse, then let it to <i>putrefy</i>. That's exactly what doesn't happen to an embalmed corpse. It seems their point is more precisely to not embalm, but let the corpse be taken by the earth and the animals.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I wasn't clear there. They sneak the body away before anyone who doesn't know better gets the chance to embalm them. I&quot;m not sure what the law is in that neck of the woods, but I presume there is some pressure to inject the chemicals.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T19:13:34-07:00","id":1466368,"title":"","content":"AFAIK embalming isn't a required process anywhere. It is too expensive to be standard, and is a fairly complex process. You don't need embalming for any standard burial, just when you have a presumption of much time passing between the death and the burial, or when you want reconstruction before the burial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T19:25:35-07:00","id":1466370,"title":"","content":"Sounds good. Still, it may be considered customary in some places. Anyway, it's a secret society, so they will have their secret rites. An archeologist who found a body in a dolmen (in the first session) was on the verge of calling the cops before one of the witches got to her and explained it was a religious choice and not murder.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}